<speak>I can see why having a defined boundary would help. We can keep the personal correspondence clearly separated from anything relating to the business, so that you are not sorting both together after a long day. I have also noted the main point for today's discussion. So your objective is to reduce the concentration in your existing holding and free up cash for your upcoming business and household commitments. Alongside that, we can cover practical matters such as where you prefer routine correspondence to reach you, how you organise it, and when you are normally available. I will keep those housekeeping items distinct in my notes, rather than putting everything into one long paragraph that is difficult to revisit.</speak>